##### [mainb] foreign=foreignD :: script catcher --help :: /usr/bin/python3.12 load_tools/catcher.py --help
usage: catcher.py [-h] --out OUT [--host HOST] [--port PORT]
                  [--control CONTROL]

A tiny SMTP catcher for the load runs (standard library only; made-up data only).

    python load_tools/catcher.py --out mail.jsonl [--host H] [--port N] [--control FILE]

Each accepted message becomes ONE line in the --out file (JSON): ts (epoch seconds), send_key (header X-Send-Key),
message_id, to (recipients joined by a comma), subject (decoded), body_sha256 (hex SHA-256 of the decoded text body
as UTF-8 with LF line ends, minus the one line break the sender adds at its end) and mode (the mode in force when it was
recorded). A message that cannot be parsed still leaves a line {"unparseable": true, ...} (the checker fails on it).
It prints `LISTENING <host> <port>` once the socket is open (use --port 0 for a free port).

Run-time mode: the CONTROL file (default `<out>.mode`) holds one word, read afresh on every command, so changing it
needs no restart. A missing or empty file means `ok`.
  ok               answer 250 as a normal server does.
  slow N           record the message, wait N seconds, then send the final 250 (N may be a decimal number).
  drop-after-data  record the message, then close the connection WITHOUT the final reply (the sender cannot tell
                   whether the mail arrived: the "maybe sent" case). The record carries mode "drop-after-data".
  reject           answer 550 to RCPT TO; nothing is recorded.
  down             close every new connection at once, without a greeting (to simulate a mail server that is
                   up but refusing; to simulate a closed port, stop the catcher).
An unknown word is treated as `ok` and noted on stderr once per change. Handles hundreds of connections at once
(asyncio, listen backlog 1024).

options:
  -h, --help         show this help message and exit
  --out OUT          JSONL file; one line per accepted message
  --host HOST
  --port PORT        0 = pick a free port (printed on stdout)
  --control CONTROL  mode file (default: <out>.mode)
exit 0
##### [mainb] foreign=foreignD :: script load_driver --help :: /usr/bin/python3.12 load_tools/load_driver.py --help
usage: load_tools.load_driver [-h] --base-url BASE_URL --scenario SCENARIO
                              --log LOG [--facts FACTS] [--workers WORKERS]
                              [--threads THREADS] [--seed SEED]
                              [--id-prefix ID_PREFIX]

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --base-url BASE_URL   desk base URL, e.g. http://127.0.0.1:8765
  --scenario SCENARIO   burst:N | rate:R:D | dupmix:TOTAL:FRACTION[:RATE]
  --log LOG             request log (JSONL), one line per intended request
  --facts FACTS         machine facts JSON (default: <log>.facts.json)
  --workers WORKERS
  --threads THREADS     threads in each worker process
  --seed SEED
  --id-prefix ID_PREFIX
                        request ids are <prefix>-<n>; change it for every run
exit 0
##### [mainb] foreign=foreignD :: script check_invariants --help :: /usr/bin/python3.12 load_tools/check_invariants.py --help
usage: load_tools.check_invariants [-h] --requests REQUESTS --book BOOK
                                   --catcher CATCHER --crm CRM --model-log
                                   MODEL_LOG [--drain DRAIN]
                                   [--model-bound MODEL_BOUND]
                                   [--max-failed MAX_FAILED]
                                   [--max-unknown MAX_UNKNOWN] [--facts FACTS]
                                   [--max-review MAX_REVIEW]
                                   [--model-required | --no-model-required]
                                   [--require-comparable | --no-require-comparable]
                                   [--max-503-rate MAX_503_RATE]
                                   [--max-drain-seconds MAX_DRAIN_SECONDS]
                                   [--json JSON]

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --requests REQUESTS   client request log (JSONL)
  --book BOOK           desk SQLite file (opened read-only)
  --catcher CATCHER     SMTP catcher log (JSONL)
  --crm CRM             CRM dump (JSON)
  --model-log MODEL_LOG
                        fake model call log (JSONL)
  --drain DRAIN         optional drain marker JSON {"drained_ts": epoch
                        seconds}; it can only make the drain later
  --model-bound MODEL_BOUND
  --max-failed MAX_FAILED
                        follow-ups allowed to end failed
  --max-unknown MAX_UNKNOWN
                        follow-ups allowed to end unknown
  --facts FACTS         driver facts JSON (default: <requests>.facts.json;
                        must exist)
  --max-review MAX_REVIEW
                        receipts allowed to end in `review`
  --model-required, --no-model-required
                        a sent lead without a model call fails (default: on if
                        the driver's facts file says the AI step was live, or
                        DESK_QUALIFIER=live_claude is in the checker's
                        environment)
  --require-comparable, --no-require-comparable
                        fail when a message or CRM row cannot be compared with
                        its lead (no recipient, subject, text hash, or empty
                        CRM record). Default ON: this command reads fake and
                        dry runs, where the catcher and the fake CRM record
                        all of them. Pass --no-require-comparable only for a
                        log from a real mailbox.
  --max-503-rate MAX_503_RATE
  --max-drain-seconds MAX_DRAIN_SECONDS
  --json JSON           write the JSON result here (default: print it after
                        the table)
exit 0
